@startuml uc002-analysis-classes
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
hide empty members
hide circle
title UC-002 Prepare benchmark dataset: analysis classes (BCE)

class "Benchmark File Reader" as BFR <<boundary>> {
  read text(path)
}
class "Prepare Benchmark" as Prep <<control>> {
  load(path)
}
class "Problem List" as PL <<entity>> {
  problems, in file order
}
class "Benchmark Error" as BE <<entity>> {
  path
  problems
}

package "Benchmark aggregate" {
  class "Benchmark" as B <<entity>> {
    id
    name
    test cases, in file order
  }
  class "Test Case" as TC <<entity>> {
    id
    question
    expected answer
  }
}

Prep --> BFR : reads through
Prep --> PL : adds each problem to
Prep --> TC : creates
Prep --> B : creates, when no problems
Prep --> BE : raises, when any problem
BE --> PL : reports
B *-- "1..*" TC : contains

note bottom of B
  Aggregate root. Invariants:
  id and name are non-empty strings;
  at least one test case;
  case ids are unique within the benchmark;
  no field the schema does not know.
end note
note right of Prep
  Business rule: checking does not stop
  at the first problem (AC-002-08).
end note
@enduml
